# TEMPLATE for .private/redact-map.tsv. Copy it there and replace every example value with a real one.
# The real file is never committed (.private/ is git-ignored).
#
# Format: one rule per line, <python regex> TAB <replacement>. Lines starting with # are comments.
# Rules run top to bottom, so put specific entries (a full IP, a full hostname) before broad ones
# (a network prefix, a short name). Every regex is also a pattern the pre-commit guard refuses to commit.
# Escape dots (\.) so the regex matches only the literal value. (?i) makes a rule case-insensitive.
#
# Values below are fake (RFC 5737 / example.com). Replace them; keep the placeholders on the right,
# because the committed files already use them.
#
# --- server A (and later B): addresses, network, IPv6, hostname, short hostname -------------------
203\.0\.113\.10	<SERVER_A_IP>
203\.0\.113\.0/24	<SERVER_A_NET>/24
203\.0\.113\.	<SERVER_A_NET>.
2001:db8::10	<SERVER_A_IPV6>
abcd\.l\.provider\.example	<SERVER_A_HOST>
abcd	srvA
# --- Reality camouflage site (a neighbour's site today) ---------------------------------------------
203\.0\.113\.6\b	<CAMOUFLAGE_A_IP>
neighbour-site\.example	<CAMOUFLAGE_A>
# --- employer: VPN portal and gateway, MDM, network, name, e-mail -----------------------------------
198\.51\.100\.163	<EMPLOYER_GP_PORTAL_IP>
198\.51\.100\.	<EMPLOYER_NET>
(?i)vpn\.corp\.example	<EMPLOYER_GP_PORTAL>
(?i)gw\.corp\.example	<EMPLOYER_GP_GATEWAY>
(?i)corp\.mdm\.example	<EMPLOYER_MDM>
(?i)user@corp\.example	<USER_EMAIL>
(?i)\bExampleCorp\b	the employer
# --- people and places: user's login and first name, the Russian PC's town, ISP, ASN ---------------
(?i)jdoe	<USER>
\bJohn\b	the user
\bSometown\b	<RU-PC town>
(?i)\bExampleNet\b	<RU-PC ISP>
AS64500	<RU-PC ASN>
